  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "For the buns, peel the potatoes and boil them for 25 minutes.",
      "timerMinutes": 25
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain the water, then add the eggs, nutmeg, pepper and salt and blend everything with a hand blender."
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the mixture has cooled, shape 4 flat bun halves and air-fry them at 160 °C for 20 minutes on each side.",
      "timerMinutes": 20
    },
    {
      "text": "For the burger sauce, finely chop the gherkins and chilli and mix with the mayonnaise, tomato paste, balsamic vinegar, honey, oregano, pepper and salt."
    },
    {
      "text": "For the wedges, wash the potatoes, cut them into quarters and put them in a bowl. Add the oil and spices and air-fry at 200 °C for 20 minutes, turning halfway through.",
      "timerMinutes": 20
    },
    {
      "text": "Wash the lettuce and separate the leaves from the stalk. Peel the onion and cut into rings. Slice the tomato."
    },
    {
      "text": "Fry the bacon in a pan until crisp, then lay it on kitchen paper.",
      "timerMinutes": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Shape the mince into four equal patties and put them in the pan with the bacon fat. Turn after 3–4 minutes.",
      "timerMinutes": 3
    },
    {
      "text": "Finally, top the patties with cheddar and cover the pan with a lid so the cheese melts.",
      "timerMinutes": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "Spread the sauce on the bottom bun halves and add lettuce, then stack 2 patties and the bacon on each. Top with onion rings and tomato slices and finish with the other bun half."
    }
  ]
